-- the critical points of the electron density, by index: a nucleus (a maximum), a bond critical point,
-- a ring critical point, a cage critical point. The molecular graph is read off them: a bond is the
-- pair of gradient paths from a bond critical point to two nuclei, so Mol's bond relation is a
-- topological invariant of the density at given nuclear positions, not an assumption.
data Crit = crit-nucleus | crit-bond | crit-ring | crit-cage
